Problem: Maximum K to Sort a Permutation (LC 3644)

Pattern: Bit Manipulation — Bitwise AND

Approach:

1. Initialize `ans = -1` to start with all bits set.
2. Traverse the array using index `i`.
3. If `nums[i] != i`, the element is misplaced.
4. Perform `ans &= nums[i]` for every misplaced element to keep only common set bits.
5. Return `max(ans, 0)`. If the array is already sorted, return `0`.

Time Complexity: \\(O(n)\\)

Space Complexity: \\(O(1)\\)